-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- A number of plain days after a day (before it, if n is negative).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month a number of months later (n positive) or earlier (n negative); where that month is shorter,
-- its last day (29 February 2028 plus 12 months is 28 February 2029; fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months on from` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`the months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS `the date` n `months on from` `the start`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `years after` `the start` MEANS `the date` (n TIMES 12) `months on from` `the start`

-- A period of n months "preceding" a day is counted back from that day (s 18(1)(a) "within the preceding 2 years", (b)
-- "during the period of 3 months immediately preceding the proposed application"). The first day whose preceding n months
-- no longer reach back to an event: the day n months on from the event, unless counting back from that day lands before
-- the event (the month it lands in is shorter, so the day was cut back), in which case the day after it. A refusal on 30
-- November 2026: counting back 3 months from 28 February 2027 reaches 28 November 2026, so 30 November is still inside;
-- from 1 March 2027 it reaches 1 December 2026, so 1 March 2027 is the first day (fork F4).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day outside the` n `months preceding, for` `the event` MEANS
    IF (`the date` (0 MINUS n) `months on from` `the candidate`) `is before` `the event`
    THEN `the date` 1 `days after` `the candidate`
    ELSE `the candidate`
    WHERE
        `the candidate` MEANS `the date` n `months on from` `the event`
